// (preset, iced feature, reason). Missing memory forms and unencodable probes
// count as coverage gaps. These exceptions preserve existing presets and never
// claim complete execution support. Remove an entry when its gap closes.
[
    ("default", "SSSE3", "Legacy XMM PABSB/PABSW/PABSD and MMX SSSE3 forms have no lift (xj-6vd.14). Preserved advertising does not promise these forms."),
    ("default", "XSAVE", "XSAVE/XRSTOR have no lift (xj-6vd.16). The legacy projection supplies no leaf 0xD sizes; a custom table exposing save-area sizes can select an instruction that traps."),
    ("default", "AVX", "Some VEX shifts, shuffles and arithmetic forms remain unlifted; implicit-memory maskmov probes are also unencodable. Keep the selected preset while exposing these gaps."),
    ("default", "FPU", "Some x87 comparisons and environment/save forms remain unlifted; obsolete and short environment probes are partly unencodable. The FPU baseline remains advertised."),
    ("default", "CX8", "CMPXCHG8B has no lift. Preserve the frozen default and inherited baseline; making CX8 a Feature now lets an embedder withhold it."),
    ("default", "CMOV", "Integer CMOV lifts, but iced also tags unlifted x87 FCMOV forms with this bit. Preserve the scalar baseline and report those forms."),
    ("default", "MMX", "MMX forms remain unlifted. Preserve the detection bit used by existing CPU detection; execution of those forms still traps."),
